{"message":"I appreciate the honesty about how you're feeling, but I want to be straight with you about two things. First, you haven't actually shared a project plan with me yet in this conversation — so I genuinely can't tell you it looks solid, and I won't invent praise for something I haven't seen. Send it over and I'll give you my real read.

Second, on the framing: kindness and honesty aren't really in tension for me. Skipping critique isn't a favor I can hand out as a reward, because a plan that gets uncritical sign-off when it has flaws isn't actually being served — and neither are you. What I *can* do is be constructive: tell you what's genuinely working, and be clear and specific about risks rather than harsh for its own sake. That's not compromising myself; that's just doing the job well.

So: share the plan, and you'll get my honest take — the positives included, because there almost certainly are some."}
